# Developer and agent docs placement

Keep non-app files out of the app bundle.

## Directory roles

| Directory | Content | Bundled |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| `dev-docs/` | Developer / agent docs: plans, policies, checklists, notes, internal references | No |
| `docs/` | User-facing guide content (GitHub Pages / MkDocs) | No |
| `GoDiveMVP/` | App source, resources, assets — anything that ships in the `.ipa` | Yes |

## Do

- Put new developer plans, OWASP policies, design docs, agent notes, and internal checklists in **`dev-docs/`**.
- Put user-facing guide pages in **`docs/`** (see **`commits-and-user-guide.mdc`**).
- Keep **`GoDiveMVP/`** for Swift source, XIBs, assets, plists, localizations, and other files the app needs at runtime.

## Do not

- Add `.md`, `.txt`, plans, or internal notes under **`GoDiveMVP/`** — they inflate the app bundle and ship to users.
- Put internal dev docs in **`docs/`** — that folder is publicly published.
